WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
Two children.

2
00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:02.600
Same puzzles.

3
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:03.930
Both do well.

4
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.090
One hears: you must be really clever.

5
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.400
The other: you must
have worked really hard.

6
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.770
Next, both get puzzles
that are far too hard.

7
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.070
Both struggle.

8
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.050
Then easy puzzles again.

9
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.470
And in experiments like this, the children
praised for being clever tend to do

10
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.490
worse.

11
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.240
Praise is meant to help.

12
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.540
So why would calling a
child clever backfire?

13
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:32.010
In this mission, you'll meet two beliefs
about whether your abilities can change:

14
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.940
a fixed mindset and a growth mindset.

15
00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:38.490
And you'll compare person
praise with praise for effort.

16
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: explain why calling a
child clever can make them do worse.
